# What EAS Build uploads from this repo. Read from the repo root and used
# INSTEAD of .gitignore. EAS does not apply the nested .gitignore files in
# apps/*, so without this it uploaded the backend's .env (Gemini key), its
# Python .venv and a local android/ folder (2026-10-04).
#
# Allowlist: upload only the mobile app's source. (No trailing slashes on the
# "!" lines: EAS's matcher then fails to re-include the folders.)
/*
!/apps
/apps/*
!/apps/mobile

# Generated or local-only inside the app. android/ and ios/ must not be
# uploaded, or EAS builds a stale local copy instead of running prebuild.
/apps/mobile/node_modules
/apps/mobile/android
/apps/mobile/ios
/apps/mobile/.expo
/apps/mobile/dist
/apps/mobile/web-build

# Secrets, anywhere (belt and braces)
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/*.p8
**/*.p12
**/*.key
**/*.pem
